    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for libmodplug",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for libmodplug fixes the following issues:\n\nChanges in libmodplug:\n\n- CVE-2026-108577: This issue affects the function abc_add_gchord of the file src/load_abc.cpp of the component ABC Music Format Parser. This manipulation causes resource consumption [bsc#1284977]\n- CVE-2026-111270: a heap-based out-of-bounds write in CSoundFile:ReadDSM() in src/load_dsm.cpp because nPat is never checked against MAX_PATTERNS [bsc#1285765]\n- CVE-2026-111271: a heap-based out-of-bounds read vulnerability in CSoundFile:ReadAMS2() in src/load_ams.cpp [bsc#1285766]\n- CVE-2026-75904: libmodplug through 0.8.9.1 contains an out-of-bounds read in pat_smplooped in src/load_pat.cpp [bsc#1275624]\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "openSUSE-Leap-16.0-packagehub-691",
        "title": "Patchnames"
